// Chapter — a saga chapter ability as data [CR#714.2b]: "{rN}—[Effect]"
// means "When one or more lore counters are put onto this Saga, if the
// number of lore counters on it was less than N and became at least N,
// [effect]." `OneOrMore` matches the placement BATCH once ([CR#603.3b]),
// and `Crossed` is [CR#714.2b]'s was-less-than/became-at-least gate
// verbatim, read off the fired fact's before/after channel — a
// counter-doubled 0→2 jump (Doubling Season) is ONE fact whose crossing
// chapters I and II each observe (and chapter III does not). The Saga
// subtype registry row (types/enchantment/Saga.ron) confers the
// enters-with-counter Also [CR#714.3a], the turn-based lore increment
// [CR#714.3c] and the final-chapter sacrifice [CR#714.4], whose final chapter
// number is the greatest threshold among these ([CR#714.2d]).
//
// `n` is ONE OR MORE chapter numbers ([CR#714.2c] — a range "{rN1}, {rN2}—"
// fires the same effect at each), spliced into `Crossed`'s `thresholds`
// list; a single chapter is a one-element list (`n: [1]`).
//
// The inner ability is a PLAIN, REMOVABLE `Triggered` — NOT `Innate`. A
// chapter ability is the card's printed ability ([CR#714.2] "a chapter
// symbol is a keyword ability that represents a triggered ability"), and
// [CR#714.2d] contemplates a Saga that has lost its chapter abilities
// (final chapter number 0) — exactly what layer-6 ability removal produces.
// `Innate` (rule-of-the-object, removal-immune) stays only on the Saga
// subtype-conferred rules, never on chapters.
//
// Usage: Chapter(n: [2], effect: <chapter effect>) /
//        Chapter(n: [1, 2], effect: <chapter effect>).
(
    name: "Chapter",
    template: "${n} — ${effect}",
    kinds: [Ability],
    params: { "n": Counts, "effect": OneShotEffect },
    body: Triggered(
        event: OneOrMore(CounterPlaced(kind: LoreCounter, on: Ref(This))),
        condition: Crossed(
            value: CounterCount(This, LoreCounter),
            thresholds: Param(n),
        ),
        effect: Param(effect),
    ),
)
